        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4725aff0-6668-5d5a-841e-660973b81dc1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ash Naylor, Ashley Naylor, Matthew Cotter, Wally Kempton, Wally Meanie\n- Bands: Even, Incubus\n- Places: Australia, Melbourne, Calabasas, California\n- Songs: “Megalomaniac”\n- Albums: Less Is More, Come Again, A Different High, Free Kicks, Even, In Another Time, A Crow Left of the Murder...\n\nFacts:\n- Even is an Australian indie rock three-piece formed in March 1994.\n- Even is fronted by singer-songwriter-guitarist Ash Naylor, with Matthew Cotter on drums and Wally Kempton, also known as Wally Meanie, on bass guitar and backing vocals.\n- Even played regularly on the live music scene and toured nationally and internationally.\n- Even released the studio album “Less Is More” on 10 June 1996.\n- Even released the studio album “Come Again” on 28 September 1998.\n- Even released the studio album “A Different High” on 14 May 2001.\n- “Megalomaniac” is a song by the American rock band Incubus from the 2004 album “A Crow Left of the Murder...”.\n- “Megalomaniac” was released as a single in December 2003 and reached number one on Billboard’s Modern Rock Tracks for six weeks.\n- Even released the studio album “Free Kicks” on 6 June 2004.\n- Even released the self-titled studio album “Even” on 29 March 2008.\n- Even released the studio album “In Another Time” on 9 December 2011.\n- Incubus is an American rock band from Calabasas, California.\n- Ashley Naylor is an Australian musician best known for guitar and vocals in the Melbourne-based band Even.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8fbe8ddf-d08f-51dd-b0f9-a7aa6cea31cc",
        "text": "Page: Even (band). Sentence: Even are an Australian indie rock three-piece fronted by singer-songwriter-guitarist, Ash Naylor, with Matthew Cotter on drums and Wally Kempton (also known as Wally Meanie) on bass guitar and backing vocals.\nPage: Even (band). Sentence: They formed in March 1994 and played regularly around the live music scene and toured both nationally and internationally.\nPage: Even (band). Sentence: They have released six studio albums, \"Less Is More\" (10 June 1996), \"Come Again\" (28 September 1998), \"A Different High\" (14 May 2001), \"Free Kicks\" (6 June 2004), \"Even\" (29 March 2008) and \"In Another Time\" (9 December 2011).\nPage: Incubus (band). Sentence: Incubus is an American rock band from Calabasas, California.\nPage: Ashley Naylor. Sentence: Ashley Naylor is an Australian musician, best known for his guitar and vocals in Melbourne-based band Even.\nPage: Megalomaniac (Incubus song). Sentence: \"Megalomaniac\" is a song by the American rock band Incubus, from their 2004 album \"A Crow Left of the Murder...\" It was released as a single in December 2003, and eventually reached the top of \"Billboard\"' s Modern Rock Tracks, where it stayed for a six-week period.",
